Of the 56 past prime ministers, five served more than 7 years while twenty-six served less than a year. [[Juichi Miyazaki]] became the first Prime Minister of Mitoyagi in 1872 and is the only person to have served on four separate occasions. [[Enoki Kanezane]] is the longest-serving prime minister with over ten years on two separate occasions, while [[Michio Watanabe]] is the shortest-serving at 44 days. [[Yasuhiro Nakasone]] was the longest-serving prime minister in the Federal Republic period (1970–2011).

